      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "# Engineering Release Plan: Authentication Flow v2.0\n\n**Owner:** Auth Team Lead\n**Status:** Draft / Pending Security Review\n**Target Release Date:** [Insert Date]\n**Jira Epic:** AUTH-2024-001\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nThis document outlines the deployment strategy for migrating from our legacy session-based authentication to the new OAuth 2.0/OIDC compliant flow. The primary goals are to improve security posture, enable SSO integration, and reduce login latency by 40%. This is a high-risk change affecting 100% of user entry points, requiring a conservative, staged rollout with immediate rollback capabilities.\n\n## 2. Pre-Release Prerequisites\n\n### 2.1 Security Review\n*   **Threat Modeling:** Completed. Identified risks: Token leakage, CSRF, Session fixation. Mitigations implemented (HttpOnly cookies, SameSite=Lax, PKCE).\n*   **Penetration Testing:** Scheduled for [Date]. Must pass with zero Critical/High findings before production rollout begins.\n*   **Dependency Audit:** All new auth libraries (e.g., `passport`, `oidc-client`) scanned for CVEs. No known vulnerabilities.\n\n### 2.2 Feature Flags\nWe will use [LaunchDarkly/ConfigCat/Custom Flag Service] to control visibility.\n*   `auth_v2_enabled`: Global kill switch. Default: `false`.\n*   `auth_v2_percentage`: Controls rollout percentage. Default: `0`.\n*   `auth_v2_user_whitelist`: List of internal employee emails for dogfooding.\n*   `auth_v2_legacy_fallback`: If `true`, users failing new auth are silently redirected to legacy flow. Default: `true` during initial rollout.\n\n## 3. Migration Strategy\n\n### 3.1 Data Migration\n*   **User Credentials:** No password migration required (hashes remain compatible).\n*   **Session Store:** New flow uses JWTs stored in HttpOnly cookies. Legacy sessions (Redis) will coexist.\n*   **Backfill:** No schema changes required. New `auth_version` column added to `users` table (default: `v1`). Will be updated to `v2` upon successful first login via new flow.\n\n### 3.2 Backward Compatibility\n*   Legacy API endpoints (`/api/v1/login`) remain active for 90 days.\n*"
      },
      "finish_reason": "length"
    }
  ],
